<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A fridge costs Ksh <m>{42\,000}</m> cash. On hire purchase you pay a deposit of <m>{10}\%</m> of the cash price and <m>{12}</m> monthly instalments of Ksh <m>{3600}</m>.</p><p>(a) Find the deposit.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) Find the hire purchase price.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans2"/>  </p><p>(c) How much more than the cash price is this?</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans3"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Deposit <m>= \dfrac{ {10} }{100} \times {42\,000} = {4200}</m>.</p><p>(b) The instalments total <m>{12} \times {3600} = {43\,200}</m>. Hire purchase price <m>=</m> deposit <m>+</m> instalments <m>= {4200} + {43\,200} = {47\,400}</m>.</p><p>(c) <m>{47\,400} - {42\,000} = {5400}</m>. You use the goods now and pay more than the cash price.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>4200</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>47400</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>5400</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>